{"type":"user","uuid":"298c6d9d-b935-4b55-94f8-423f9bedbeb3","session_id":"a85e2138-3a1f-423a-b9c7-c1557cf8f76e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89aa60b69e13ebee","is_error":false,"content":"/*\n * SkyTube\n * Copyright (C) 2019  Zsombor Gegesy\n *\n * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify\n * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by\n * the Free Software Foundation (version 3 of the License).\n *\n * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\n * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\n * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\n * GNU General Public License for more details.\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License\n * along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.\n */\npackage free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.YouTube.newpipe;\n\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.InfoItem;\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.ListExtractor;\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.StreamingService;\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.channel.ChannelInfoItem;\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.exceptions.ParsingException;\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.linkhandler.LinkHandlerFactory;\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.playlist.PlaylistInfoItem;\nimport org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.stream.StreamInfoItem;\n\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Collections;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.Logger;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.YouTube.POJOs.CardData;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.YouTube.POJOs.YouTubeChannel;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.YouTube.POJOs.YouTubePlaylist;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.YouTube.POJOs.YouTubeVideo;\n\npublic class VideoPager extends Pager<InfoItem, CardData> {\n    private final Set<String> seenVideos = new HashSet<>();\n\n    public VideoPager(StreamingService streamingService, ListExtractor<? extends InfoItem> channelExtractor) {\n        super(streamingService, channelExtractor);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    protected List<CardData> extract(ListExtractor.InfoItemsPage<? extends InfoItem> page) throws NewPipeException {\n        List<CardData> result = new ArrayList<>(page.getItems().size());\n        if (NewPipeService.DEBUG_LOG) {\n            Logger.d(this, \"extract from %s, items: %s\", page, page.getItems().size());\n        }\n        int repeatCounter = 0;\n        int unexpected = 0;\n\n        for (InfoItem infoItem : page.getItems()) {\n            if (infoItem instanceof StreamInfoItem) {\n                String id = getId(streamLinkHandler, infoItem.getUrl());\n                StreamInfoItem streamInfo = (StreamInfoItem) infoItem;\n                if (seenVideos.contains(id)) {\n                    repeatCounter++;\n                } else {\n                    seenVideos.add(id);\n                    result.add(convert(streamInfo, id));\n                }\n            } else if (infoItem instanceof PlaylistInfoItem) {\n                PlaylistInfoItem playlistInfoItem = (PlaylistInfoItem) infoItem;\n                result.add(convert(playlistInfoItem, getId(playlistLinkHandler, infoItem.getUrl())));\n            } else if (infoItem instanceof ChannelInfoItem) {\n                ChannelInfoItem channelInfoItem = (ChannelInfoItem) infoItem;\n                result.add(convert(channelInfoItem));\n            } else {\n                Logger.i(this, \"Unexpected item %s, type:%s\", infoItem, infoItem.getClass());\n                unexpected ++;\n            }\n        }\n        if (NewPipeService.DEBUG_LOG) {\n            Logger.d(this, \"From the requested %s, number of duplicates: %s, wrong types: %s\", page.getItems().size(), repeatCounter, unexpected);\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private String getId(LinkHandlerFactory handler, String url) throws NewPipeException {\n        try {\n            return handler.getId(url);\n        } catch (ParsingException e) {\n            throw new NewPipeException(\"Unable to convert \" + url + \" with \" + handler, e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public List<YouTubeVideo> getNextPageAsVideos() throws NewPipeException {\n        List<CardData> cards = getNextPage();\n        List<YouTubeVideo> result = new ArrayList<>(cards.size());\n        for (CardData cardData: cards) {\n            if (cardData instanceof YouTubeVideo) {\n                result.add((YouTubeVideo) cardData);\n            }\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    protected YouTubeVideo convert(StreamInfoItem item, String id) {\n        NewPipeService.DateInfo date = new NewPipeService.DateInfo(item.getUploadDate());\n        if (NewPipeService.DEBUG_LOG) {\n            Logger.i(this, \"item %s, title=%s at %s\", id, item.getName(), date);\n        }\n        YouTubeChannel ch = new YouTubeChannel(item.getUploaderUrl(), item.getUploaderName());\n        return new YouTubeVideo(id, item.getName(), null, item.getDuration(), ch,\n                item.getViewCount(), date.instant, date.exact, NewPipeService.getThumbnailUrl(id));\n    }\n\n    private CardData convert(PlaylistInfoItem playlistInfoItem, String id) {\n        return new YouTubePlaylist(id, playlistInfoItem.getName(), \"\", null, playlistInfoItem.getStreamCount(), NewPipeUtils.getThumbnailUrl(playlistInfoItem),\n                null);\n    }\n\n    private CardData convert(ChannelInfoItem channelInfoItem) {\n        String url = channelInfoItem.getUrl();\n        String id = getId(url);\n        return new YouTubeChannel(id, channelInfoItem.getName(), channelInfoItem.getDescription(), NewPipeUtils.getThumbnailUrl(channelInfoItem), null,\n                channelInfoItem.getSubscriberCount(), false, -1, System.currentTimeMillis(), null, Collections.emptyList());\n    }\n\n    private String getId(String url) {\n        try {\n            return channelLinkHandler.getId(url);\n        } catch (ParsingException p) {\n            Logger.e(this, \"Unable to parse channel url \"+ url, p);\n            return url;\n        }\n    }\n\n}\n"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"b37ee1f3-5947-4d73-9cec-7a847281ed6a","session_id":"a85e2138-3a1f-423a-b9c7-c1557cf8f76e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"b37ee1f3-5947-4d73-9cec-7a847281ed6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so the `id` in `VideoPager.extract()` is obtained from:\n```java\nString id = getId(streamLinkHandler, infoItem.getUrl());\n```\n\nWhere `getId()` calls `streamLinkHandler.getId(url)`. This should extract the actual video ID from the URL.\n\nBut wait, looking at `convert(ChannelInfoItem channelInfoItem)`:\n```java\nprivate CardData convert(ChannelInfoItem channelInfoItem) {\n    String url = channelInfoItem.getUrl();\n    String id = getId(url);\n    return new YouTubeChannel(id, channelInfoItem.getName(), ...);\n}\n```\n\nThis converts ChannelInfoItem to a YouTubeChannel, not a YouTubeVideo. And then in `VideoPagerWithChannel.getChannelVideos()`, if the list includes channel items mixed with video items, the `getNextPageAsVideos()` method only returns items that are instances of `YouTubeVideo`. So that should be fine.\n\nOK, I think I've been overcomplicating this. Let me re-examine the problem from the bug report:\n\nThe bug report says:\n- The url of a video, which you receive to share is not valid.\n- It just contains the channel.\n- Example invalid url: `https://www.youtube.com/https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKvfzCyVQPe2IYg4PkugvWQ`\n\nThe key phrase is \"the url of a video, which you receive to share\". This means the user received a video URL via an intent (from another app's \"share\" feature), and when they try to copy that video's URL, it's invalid.\n\nNow let me trace the flow:\n1. User receives a share intent with a video URL\n2. `MainActivity` opens and passes the URL to `YouTubePlayerV1Fragment`\n\n\n3. In `onCreateView`, if `youTubeVideo` is null, it calls `SkyTubeApp.getUrlFromIntent(requireContext(), requireActivity().getIntent())` to extract the ContentId, then uses `YouTubeTasks.getVideoDetails()` to fetch video information\n\nThe problem likely lies in how the video URL is being processed or stored during this intent-handling flow. I need to complete the partial thought from the current rewritten thinking first. The sentence ends mid-word at \"B\", so I'll finish it using the next thinking:\n\nB. When `copyurl` is clicked, `youTubeVideo.copyUrl()` calls `SkyTubeApp.copyUrl(context, \"Video URL\", getVideoUrl())`. This calls `YouTubeVideo.getVideoUrl()` which returns `String.format(\"https://youtu.be/%s\", id)`. If `id` is null, the URL becomes `\"https://youtu.be/null\"`.\n\nBut wait, the bug URL is `https://www.youtube.com/https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKvfzCyVQPe2IYg4PkugvWQ`. This doesn't match `https://youtu.be/null`. Let me reconsider...\n\nThe bug URL format `https://www.youtube.com/https://www.youtube.com/channel/...` suggests two URLs concatenated:\n1. `https://www.youtube.com/` - some base URL\n2. `https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKvfzCyVQPe2IYg4PkugvWQ` - the channel URL\n\nActually, wait. I think the user might be misinterpreting the URL or there's a URL concatenation bug. Let me look more carefully at the bug report:\n\n\"To Reproduce\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\n1. Go to any youtube video\n2. Click on the three points\n3. Click Copy Url\n4. Paste the url somewhere\n5. See invalid url\"\n\nThe user goes to a YouTube video, clicks three dots (share menu), clicks \"Copy Url\", and pastes it somewhere, seeing an invalid URL.\n\nThe expected behavior is `https://youtu.be/7MoipvBda_8` or `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7MripvBda_8`.\n\nSo the expected is a video URL, but the actual is a channel URL. The issue is that `getVideoUrl()` returns a channel URL instead of a video URL. This means `id` must contain the channel ID, not the video ID. Looking at the second YouTubeVideo constructor, `this.id = id` should set it to the video ID from `NewPipeService.getDetails()`, but something's going wrong in the URL generation. The constructor signature is correct with `videoId` as the first parameter, so I need to trace where the channel URL is actually coming from in `getVideoUrl()` instead.\n\nLooking at `SkyTubeApp.copyUrl()`, it takes a text label and URL string, creates a clip with that URL, and shows a toast confirmation. The issue might be in how the URL is being constructed or passed before it reaches this method.\n\nChecking `getVideoUrl()`, it formats the video URL using the `id` field. But the bug shows a channel URL, not a video URL, so something else must be generating that URL—possibly through the intent handling path in `getUrlFromIntent()` which extracts URLs from shared content. Looking at the `parse` method, when it extracts the content ID, it calls `handler.getUrl(id)` to generate the canonical URL, which for a video should be the standard YouTube watch URL. Then `getDetails` retrieves the full video information using that ID.\n\nThe `getVideoUrl()` method in `NewPipeService` constructs the video URL by asking the service's stream link handler for the URL corresponding to a given video ID. Both of these should be producing the correct watch URL format, so the issue must lie elsewhere in how the URL is being processed or displayed.\n\nLooking at `ExternalUrlActivity`, it receives an intent with a URL and attempts to parse it. If parsing succeeds, it opens the content; if not, it launches the URL in an external browser. The flow seems sound, but I'm wondering if the problem might be in how `ContentId` stores and passes the URL through the system.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
