{"type":"assistant","uuid":"68ab1db2-b3c9-4806-b195-e7eb5f34f57a","session_id":"a85e2138-3a1f-423a-b9c7-c1557cf8f76e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"68ab1db2-b3c9-4806-b195-e7eb5f34f57a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe project builds successfully. Here's a summary of the bug and fix:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause:** The `ChannelActionHandler.handleChannelActions()` method was intercepting the `R.id.copyurl` menu item before the video player's own handler could process it.\n\n**Bug Flow:**\n1. User opens a video in SkyTube's video player\n2. User taps the menu (three dots) and selects \"Copy URL\"\n3. `YouTubePlayerV1Fragment.onOptionsItemSelected()` is called\n4. It first calls `actionHandler.handleChannelActions(getContext(), youTubeChannel, item.getItemId())`\n5. `ChannelActionHandler` matches `R.id.copyurl` and copies `channel.getChannelUrl()` (the **channel** URL) instead of the video URL\n6. The video player's `case R.id.copyurl: youTubeVideo.copyUrl(getContext())` is **never reached**\n\n**Affected Components:**\n- `YouTubePlayerV1Fragment` — video player (V1)\n- `YouTubePlayerV2Fragment` — video player (V2)  \n- `GridViewHolder` — video grid options menu\n\nAll three call `handleChannelActions()` before their own `copyurl` handler, causing the channel URL to be copied instead of the video URL.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/free/rm/skytube/gui/businessobjects/views/ChannelActionHandler.java`\n\n**Change:** Removed the `R.id.copyurl` case from `handleChannelActions()`. This allows `R.id.copyurl` to fall through to the video-specific handlers (`youTubeVideo.copyUrl()`), which correctly copy the video URL via `getVideoUrl()` → `\"https://youtu.be/{videoId}\"`."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":101215,"output_tokens":382,"cache_read_input_tokens":100608,"total_tokens":101597}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"b30b5c0a-ad8e-425e-b0c2-5e3061c12ec8","session_id":"a85e2138-3a1f-423a-b9c7-c1557cf8f76e","is_error":false,"duration_ms":206874,"duration_api_ms":163801,"num_turns":43,"result":"\n\nThe project builds successfully. Here's a summary of the bug and fix:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause:** The `ChannelActionHandler.handleChannelActions()` method was intercepting the `R.id.copyurl` menu item before the video player's own handler could process it.\n\n**Bug Flow:**\n1. User opens a video in SkyTube's video player\n2. User taps the menu (three dots) and selects \"Copy URL\"\n3. `YouTubePlayerV1Fragment.onOptionsItemSelected()` is called\n4. It first calls `actionHandler.handleChannelActions(getContext(), youTubeChannel, item.getItemId())`\n5. `ChannelActionHandler` matches `R.id.copyurl` and copies `channel.getChannelUrl()` (the **channel** URL) instead of the video URL\n6. The video player's `case R.id.copyurl: youTubeVideo.copyUrl(getContext())` is **never reached**\n\n**Affected Components:**\n- `YouTubePlayerV1Fragment` — video player (V1)\n- `YouTubePlayerV2Fragment` — video player (V2)  \n- `GridViewHolder` — video grid options menu\n\nAll three call `handleChannelActions()` before their own `copyurl` handler, causing the channel URL to be copied instead of the video URL.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/free/rm/skytube/gui/businessobjects/views/ChannelActionHandler.java`\n\n**Change:** Removed the `R.id.copyurl` case from `handleChannelActions()`. This allows `R.id.copyurl` to fall through to the video-specific handlers (`youTubeVideo.copyUrl()`), which correctly copy the video URL via `getVideoUrl()` → `\"https://youtu.be/{videoId}\"`.","usage":{"input_tokens":3172038,"output_tokens":25008,"cache_read_input_tokens":3014048,"total_tokens":3197046},"permission_denials":[]}
